  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:12.0pt;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The development would result in the loss of a high quality,\r\n3-bedroom single family dwelling house by replacing it with a poor standard of\r\naccommodation for the occupiers, comprising of (i) gross internal floor areas and\r\nbedroom areas which fail to comply with minimum space standards, and (ii) a bedroom\r\nplaced within the inappropriate setting of a conservatory, which fails to\r\nprovide high quality amenity for the future occupier. The proposals would be\r\ncontrary to policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), policies 20, 56, 57 of\r\nWaltham Forests Local Development Plan LP1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:12.0pt;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Nowithstanding the first reason for refusal, the application\r\nas submitted comprises of inconsistent plans and insufficient detailing,\r\nrelating to (i) the re-configuration and re-build of the conservatory. As such\r\nit is not possible to establish that the development complies with policies 20,\r\n56, 57 of Waltham Forests Local Development Plan LP1 (2024)&amp;nbsp; and Waltham Forests’ Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument &#x27;Urban Design (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
